{"id":"176e427014394578","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-mv-algebra-gap.md","title":"thm-mv-algebra-gap","display":"thm-mv-algebra-gap","type":"theorem","metadata":{"book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","depends_on":["[[93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus]]"],"display":"thm-mv-algebra-gap","label":"93-thm-mv-algebra-gap","aliases":["93-thm-mv-algebra-gap"],"type":"theorem"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ba86732612230e2a\" href=\"?note=ba86732612230e2a\" title=\"93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus\">93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus</a></span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-mv-algebra-gap"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-mv-algebra-gap"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-mv-algebra-gap</span></div>"},{"key":"type","html":"theorem"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-mv-algebra-gap-thm-mv-algebra-gap\">thm-mv-algebra-gap <code>thm-mv-algebra-gap</code></h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LukPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L)\">\\(\\mathrm{LukPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L)\\)</span> is the four-scheme infinite-valued Łukasiewicz presentation of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ba86732612230e2a\" href=\"?note=ba86732612230e2a\" title=\"93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus\">93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\">\\(F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\)</span> is the shared implication-negation formula carrier, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vdash^{\\mathsf L_{\\infty}}_{93}\">\\(\\vdash^{\\mathsf L_{\\infty}}_{93}\\)</span> is the proof-induced relation, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models^{[0,1]}_{93}\">\\(\\models^{[0,1]}_{93}\\)</span> is validity in the explicitly defined standard real truth algebra.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}mv\\text{-}algebra\\text{-}gap}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LukPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L)\\to\n\\forall\\varphi\\in F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\varnothing\\vdash^{\\mathsf L_{\\infty}}_{93}\\varphi\n\\leftrightarrow\\models^{[0,1]}_{93}\\varphi\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}mv\\text{-}algebra\\text{-}gap}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LukPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L)\\to\n\\forall\\varphi\\in F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\varnothing\\vdash^{\\mathsf L_{\\infty}}_{93}\\varphi\n\\leftrightarrow\\models^{[0,1]}_{93}\\varphi\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>This is standard completeness for theoremhood. The proof calculus, its signature, and the real truth algebra are now formal objects rather than prose names. The statement does not assert strong completeness of the single standard algebra for arbitrary infinite premise sets.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-mv-algebra-gap-thm-mv-algebra-gap","text":"thm-mv-algebra-gap `thm-mv-algebra-gap`","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"ba86732612230e2a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus","status":"resolved","id":"ba86732612230e2a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LukPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L)$ is the four-scheme infinite-valued Łukasiewicz presentation of [[93-df-lukasiewicz-propositional-calculus]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{LukPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L)","display":false},{"tex":"F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\vdash^{\\mathsf L_{\\infty}}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\models^{[0,1]}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}mv\\text{-}algebra\\text{-}gap}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LukPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P,\\mathsf L)\\to\n\\forall\\varphi\\in F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\varnothing\\vdash^{\\mathsf L_{\\infty}}_{93}\\varphi\n\\leftrightarrow\\models^{[0,1]}_{93}\\varphi\\Bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1240,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["ba86732612230e2a"]}